    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.07,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.75,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings stall at about 0.97–1.0 from 6 h to 18 h. That flat ceiling is what a saturated reader would produce. A 10-fold dilution of the 18 h aliquot read 0.107, which is 1.07 once multiplied back. That is higher than the undiluted 0.972. The dilution is in the reader's more linear range, so the true biomass is probably above the undiluted reading. The difference is only about 10%, and I could afford just one replicate, so the evidence is limited. If the reader were saturating more severely, the diluted reading would likely scale back to a much larger value. I therefore put my confidence at about 0.75."
